{"shortDescription":"Spot fuel oil premiums were broadly steady in Asia on Monday, while more sale tenders from Southeast Asian exporters closed.Some trades for 380-cst high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) emerged at largely rangebound premiums from the previous session, while trade for very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) was br…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Spot fuel oil premiums were broadly steady in Asia on Monday, while more sale tenders from Southeast Asian exporters closed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some trades for 380-cst high sulphur fuel oil (HSFO) emerged at largely rangebound premiums from the previous session, while trade for very low sulphur fuel oil (VLSFO) was broadly thin."]},{"type":"p","children":["The hi-five spread (FO05-380SGMc1) retreated slightly from last week, closing at about $155.60 a metric ton on Monday, based on LSEG data."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, margins traded higher at Monday's Asia close versus the previous session. VLSFO's crack (LFO05SGBRTCMc1) closed at a premium above $22.50 a barrel, while 380-cst HSFO's crack (FO380BRTCKMc1) rose to a discount of $2 a barrel."]},{"type":"p","children":["More spot sales by Southeast Asian exporters were underway, according to market sources. Thailand's PTT offered 35,000 tons of low sulphur fuel oil (LSFO) for loading from Map Ta Phut from October 19 to 21 via its monthly tender, according to market sources."]},{"type":"p","children":["Separately, Indonesia's Pertamina offered more decant oil for loading in end-October. This comprised two cargoes, including one that will load from Balongan between from October 28 to 29, and another that will load from Balikpapan from October 30 to 31."]},{"type":"p","children":["CHINA DATA"]},{"type":"p","children":["China's fuel oil exports, which were mainly for marine fuel bunkering, fell in August to an almost two-year low, hitting about 1.21 million tons, latest customs data showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Some bunkering was hampered by weather at China's main vessel refuelling hub in Zhoushan, market sources said."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, China's fuel oil imports, which typically head to refineries and also to the marine fuel blending pool, totaled 1.3 million tons for August, up 15% month on month."]},{"type":"p","children":["Buying sentiment for fuel oil in the third quarter has improved from the second quarter but has remained capped because independent refineries still have crude import quotas to utilize."]},{"type":"p","children":["OTHER NEWS"]},{"type":"p","children":["- Oil prices slid to their lowest in more than a week on Monday as investors hoped for diplomatic progress on the Iran war due to this week's UN meeting and eyed a partial recovery in shipments from Saudi Arabia despite ongoing attacks by Yemen's Houthis."]},{"type":"p","children":["- A total of 17 commodity vessels transited the Strait of Hormuz on the weekend, down from 37 a week earlier, shipping data showed on Monday, as tension in the Gulf persisted with the US and Iran in stalemate."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Bangladesh has raised fuel prices by up to 17.4%, piling fresh pressure on consumers and businesses, as the government moved to stem mounting losses from surging global oil prices and higher shipping costs linked to the Middle East conflict."]},{"type":"p","children":["- Trading house Trafigura said on Monday it had launched Volare Shipping, which would own and operate 14 supertankers, adding that it plans to sell shares in the business before listing it on the Norwegian stock exchange next month."]},{"type":"p","children":["WINDOW TRADES"]},{"type":"p","children":["- 180-cst HSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 380-cst HSFO: Three trades."]},{"type":"p","children":["- 0.5% VLSFO: No trade."]},{"type":"p","children":["ASSESSMENTS"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","childre